    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0393" n="359" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg359"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Fava to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic">February 22,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: By a decree of January
                    26, 1897, revoking a previous decree of the 7th of the same month, the royal
                    ministry of agriculture, industry, and commerce provided for the regulation of
                    importation into Italy, by sea, of cattle, salted hides, undressed skins, raw
                    wool, horns, hoofs, and other animal products, and also the importation, by land
                    and sea, of preserved swine’s flesh.</p>
                <p>I now have the honor, in pursuance of the instructions of my Government, to
                    transmit to the Department of State a copy of the aforesaid decree, and I avail
                    myself of this occassion to offer you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fava.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d348-a1.xml" xpointer="d348-a1"/>
            </div>
